d noun\" rather than disease-specific terms, avoiding any extra rationale or validity commentary.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "- **Principle: Subtype/State-Head Span Extension**\n  - **IF** a disease name is the complement of an \"of\"-prepositional phrase, **and** the governing noun is a subtype or state noun (one denoting a variety, stage, or type of condition, or a deficiency state), **and** that governing noun carries a premodifier (an adjectival, ordinal, or numeric qualifier),\n  - **THEN** the SpecificDisease span covers the full nominal phrase, from the first character of the premodifier through the end of the disease name, not the disease name alone and not a span that begins at the head noun with its premodifier removed.\n  - **Negative constraint:** Do NOT apply this rule when:\n    - the disease name is not the complement of an \"of\"-phrase governed by a subtype or state noun (for example, a bare name in subject or object position);\n    - the governing noun is a context or population noun (for example, history, risk, incidence, cases, family). The span stays on the disease name, labeled Modifier;\n    - the head word is lexically fixed inside a proper disease name, so the whole name is already the mention;\n    - the governing subtype noun has no premodifier. The span is not extended.\n  - **Consistency check:** This rule changes only span extent for SpecificDisease mentions with subtype or state heads. It does not change the SpecificDisease, DiseaseClass, or Modifier label boundaries, and it leaves context-head frames as Modifier.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2173, "output_tokens": 3788, "output_